   "about": "A historical account of Japanese labor, agrarian, socialist, communist, and nationalist movements from the late 1910s through 1940.",
   "summary": "The continuing chapter first describes the formation of student and labor groups, suffrage campaigns, and early struggles between moderate unions, anarchists, and communists. Chapters III and IV recount the Communist Party's organization, Comintern direction, factional disputes, police arrests, political trials, and episodes of violence, alongside the creation and consolidation of socialist and agrarian parties. Chapter V compares communist and nationalist reform programs and describes socialists who moved toward national socialism, including the 1933 recantation by Sano Manabu and Nabeyama Sadachika. Chapter VI begins an account of conservative, communist, and nationalist labor organizations.",
